# Project layout and hierarchy

## Layers (top to bottom)

1. **`app/`** — Expo Router only: route files, layouts, redirects. Keep them **thin** (compose UI from `src/features/...`, wire params, no business logic).
2. **`src/`** — Implementation lives **under `src/features/`** (domain features + **`common`**). **`src/core/`** holds app shell code; env-style constants live under **`src/core/config/`** (see below). **`assets/`** stays at the repo root.

## Domain features (`src/features/<feature-name>/`)

Each product domain gets its own folder (e.g. `auth`, `kg`, `home`, `profile`, `practice`, …). **All** code that clearly belongs to that domain stays inside it. Use the same inner layout everywhere:

| Folder | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| **`components/`** | UI for this feature (including full-screen views; `app/` imports from here) |
| **`hooks/`** | Feature-only hooks (`useX`) |
| **`constants/`** | Strings, keys, static maps, thresholds for this feature only |
| **`utils/`** | Pure helpers and formatters for this feature only |
| **`services/`** | API clients, adapters, and side-effecting modules for this feature |
| **`types/`** | Types and small interfaces used only by this feature |

Split or add subfolders only when it stays easy to navigate; the rule is **locality first**: if it is owned by one feature, it does not live at `src/` root.

## Shared code — `src/features/common/`

Anything **used across multiple features** but **not** owned by a single domain goes under **`src/features/common/`**. Prefer the **same** subfolders as a domain feature:

- `src/features/common/components/`
- `src/features/common/hooks/`
- `src/features/common/constants/`
- `src/features/common/utils/`
- `src/features/common/services/`
- `src/features/common/types/`

Use the name **`common`** (not `shared`) for this tree.

## App shell and config (exceptions)

- **`src/core/`** — App bootstrap: providers, theme tokens, **`core/config/`** for API base URLs and similar env-style constants, and related wiring. Keep this thin; prefer moving reusable **product** code into `features/common` or a domain feature.
- **`src/i18n/`** — Locale JSON and translation wiring (stays next to `core` as today).
- **`assets/`** — Static assets at repo root (see `@/assets/*` alias).

Imports such as `@/config/constants` resolve to **`src/core/config/`** (see `tsconfig.json`).

## Imports

Use path aliases (`@/…`). Prefer:

- `@/features/<domain>/...` for domain code
- `@/features/common/...` for cross-feature code

Shorter aliases (`@/components/...`, `@/hooks/...`, `@/services/...`, `@/utils/...`, `@/constants/...`, `@/types/...`, `@/appStyles/...`) resolve to the matching folder under **`src/features/common/`** (see root `tsconfig.json`).
